yes i somehow managed to get my hands  on a ps5 this holiday season and boy  do i have a launch story for you from a  crazy pre-order experience where i ended  up with  two ps5s to my first impressions of the  new dual sims controller my favorite  launch games and one  thing that really surprised me all that  and more in today's video  and we're starting right now  now today we're going to talk about my  pre-order experience  the actual arrival of my ps5 the dual  sense controller  the games and then my one big surprise  now if you want to jump to any of these  points in the video i'm going to include  chapter markers down  in the description below alternatively  you'll also find links  to all these points in the video in the  timeline below  people of the internet retrorec and tour  here if we're meeting for the first time  i'm just a dad who loves games and the  stories they tell  we post videos every week here on  youtube and also stream  over on twitch so from the very moment  sony announced the price and release  date for ps5 everyone knew it was going  to be an insanely hard item to find  of course they held their showcase event  back on september 16th and also  announced the price  and release date what happened after  that was just a complete  fiasco there's really no other way to  say it sony told everyone pre-orders  would be going live the following day on  september 16th  but then walmart jumped the gun and put  theirs up early  once that happened it quickly became an  all-out free-for-all as retailers  started listing their pre-orders at  random times throughout the day  now i happened to be on twitter way too  much so i kept my eye out and was quick  on the draw  anytime i saw these go for sale the  first pre-order i managed to secure was  through  target and i think amazon's pre-orders  went up that night  and because things were so hectic i  wanted to make sure i had this thing at  launch so i went ahead and pre-ordered a  second ps5 with amazon  knowing that as launch got closer i  could always cancel if need be well as  november 12th approached i talked to my  wife's cousin who happened to be looking  for a ps5  i told him about my second pre-order and  he said he'd buy it from me so that's  why i ended up keeping both  orders now despite having two pre-orders  i still didn't get  either on launch day or even the day  after my amazon pre-order shipped the  morning of the 12th  and started out two hours away from  where i live it ended up going on a  six-day journey that saw it actually  make it into my city  only to travel further away before  finally coming back and then eventually  arriving  at my house the target pre-order  actually shipped  second but ended up arriving first which  ended up being on sunday  november 15th of course in hindsight  three days really isn't that long but in  the middle of all this i was mainly  afraid the order would be lost  completely or  stolen something crazy there were just  so many ridiculous stories online i  really wanted to have this thing in hand  in all seriousness though shout out to  all the retail and delivery workers who  are trying their best to keep things  going and what has been such a crazy  year for everyone  most people out there are just doing the  best they can so make sure you remember  that when you're dealing with any  delivery workers or retail  workers this holiday season really  anytime but especially this year  so once i finally got my ps5 the first  thing i was most anxious to see was just  how  hideous this thing looked in my office  look i love sony and the playstation  brand but initially i wasn't a huge fan  of the console design especially  compared to the ps4 which was just an  absolutely beautiful console especially  the first one  i gotta say though i found a pretty good  spot for it you can see here kind of  behind my tv but you see it poking out  just a little bit there and it's grown  on me somewhat  if you're someone who owns a pc or has  built your own pc it's much closer in  size to something like a mini itx build  or even a mid tower build  here's a picture of the ps5 next to my  fractal design  define mini c case and you can see it  actually makes the ps5 look  kind of small here of course next to any  home console though the ps5 will indeed  look like a  giant of a console once you find a good  place for it though you'll soon  quickly forget about the design anyway  and become far more concerned with how  this thing runs  both my ps4 and ps4 pro were insanely  loud at times especially with  graphically intensive games  the ps5 so far i've never heard it  except when a disk is  spinning so so far so good on that front  now let's get to the dual sense  controller which has just  blown me away video game controllers  have steadily improved and made slight  tweaks and changes to a format that  really started with the nes controller  back in 1983  shoulder buttons analog sticks rumble  these were all iterations that slightly  improve the way we play and experience  games  then in 2006 nintendo gave us something  radically different with the wii remote  it was just one of those sensations that  instantly made sense when you had it in  your hand for the first time  honestly i wasn't sure i would ever have  that feeling again of something on a  controller being  so radically different i gotta say  though the dual sense has proven me  wrong because it's  honestly incredible what this controller  can do don't get me wrong it doesn't  have that same  mass appeal like the wii but if you're a  gamer familiar with controllers  try one of these things as soon as you  can and i know right now that may be  easier said than done  but hopefully this whole pandemic will  eventually be over and ps5 will be  widely available and you can try it out  in a store somewhere  i already made a separate video talking  about how impressed i am with the free  pack in game astros playroom it's the  best showcase so far for the dual since  and also happens to be a fantastic  platformer as well  but what specifically makes the  controller so great  i want to try and paint a picture for  you guys out there because i know you  keep hearing this heck i kept hearing it  before launch  and now that i have it in my hands i  want to do the best i can to help you  all get an actual feel for what this  thing can do  so for starters the triggers sony calls  them adaptive triggers and what they're  able to do with these things just  doesn't even  feel like it should be possible so far  no game that i've played does this  better than  astros playroom so just to kind of start  as a frame of reference  imagine the ps4 trigger maybe with a  little bit more resistance to it  and then imagine that that resistance  can change imagine that the trigger can  actually push back at times then imagine  as you press down that the trigger can  actually change  its level of resistance and it's not  just a matter of resistance or  no resistance it can actually change and  alter just how much resistance you're  feeling then there's the haptics here  it's all about  subtlety from giving you a sense of tiny  raindrops in astros play room to the odd  sensation of your controller  powering up when you defeat a boss in  demon souls this thing in demon souls  guys it's so  bizarre yet satisfying and it's it's  such a small thing but it's when you  defeat a boss and then activate a new  archstone  the only way i can describe it is that  it's exactly what you would imagine a  controller would feel like  if it kind of sucked up a powerful force  into it it's not a vibration you just  kind of get this satisfying feedback  from the whole controller like it's  pushing out  a little force in every direction it's  so  incredibly subtle but that i think is  what makes it work so well  and you can't forget about the overall  build quality in general  the dual shock 4 still feels pretty good  to me but there's no denying the overall  build quality of the dual sense is far  superior then you have the dualshock 3  which honestly feels like one of my  son's plastic toy controllers at this  point it's  crazy as far as the games go i've beaten  both astros playroom as well as demon  souls and have started spider-man miles  morales  i've also played a handful of ps4 titles  on the system and have tried out some  fan favorites like fortnite and destiny  in short demon souls is absolutely a  phenomenal launch game  even though it's a remake this is one  that was absolutely warranted  i had honestly forgotten how good this  game is which is crazy considering how  big a fan i am of from software  its level design is outstanding and even  after i beat it i actually found myself  itching to dive back in for another  playthrough which i don't usually do  with the from games even though i love  them  you guys already know i think astro is  great and what i've played so far of  miles morales has been good as well  now one thing that's really surprised me  that i didn't expect and that is how  much better the ps5 makes  a lot of your old ps4 games now this  isn't a given with every game so you'll  have to look into this on a case-by-case  basis when it comes to your favorite  games  but take ghost of tsushima for example  which had both a performance mode and  fidelity mode for ps4 pro  now you can get a solid 60fps experience  in the fidelity mode when you're playing  on ps5 that's right  not the performance mode in ghost of  tsushima the fidelity mode  there's also days gone which feels like  an entirely different game now with the  rock solid frame rate  most of these games require a patch from  the devs but if there are any games that  originally had unlocked frame rates they  don't need any patch at all to see some  improvement  you'll also get a bunch of these games  right away if you're a playstation plus  member as they are part of the  playstation plus collection  god of war is another that runs better  now but they could actually make this  one even better if they patched an  update for it  right now the only way to get 60fps in  that game is to run it at its  performance mode which does drop the  resolution  now this doesn't mean that the ps5 is  incapable of running it at the higher  frame rate and higher resolution it's  just that they haven't patched it in  there  two big titles that don't see all that  much of an improvement at least right  now  are the last of us part two and of  course fan favorite  bloodborne here's to hoping we get  something in the future  on both of those as far as any downsides  go the ui is taking some time to get  used to  overall i like the look and feel of it  but there's quite a bit lacking  at the moment there are no themes or  folders certain items have moved around  from where you'd come to expect them on  ps4 and were still waiting on promise  features such as variable refresh rates  if you have an hdr supported tv you  should know the ps5 will  always run in hdr mode even when playing  ps4 games that didn't have an hdr mode  this means those ps4 games are actually  being displayed through an hdr container  now this is a departure from the ps4  which you may remember would only kick  on the hdr when loading into a game that  supported it  if you remember that little flicker of a  black screen and then the hdr logo would  pop  up or vice versa that's what was  happening there now i personally haven't  noticed a huge difference but i'm also  not comparing this side by side to my  old ps4  you should definitely take the  opportunity though to make sure your  tv's hdr mode is calibrated  to your ideal settings and ultimately if  it bothers you too much you can always  disable hdr from the ps5 menu  which then in turn will leave those old  ps4 games looking exactly like they did  on ps4 theoretically all that being said  i've certainly  enjoyed my time with the ps5 so far and  believe this generation is shaping up to  be another  amazing one for sony fans if you have  any questions at all about the ps5 let  me know down in the comments  as always thank you all so much for  watching i'll talk to you again soon
 

